# Growth: f sigma_8(z) from redshift-space distortions.
# Columns: z, f sigma_8, sigma (diagonal error), Omega_m of the survey's fiducial flat
# LCDM (used only by the Alcock-Paczynski-type correction, constants.FS8_AP_CORRECTION).
# Source: Skara & Perivolaropoulos 2020 (arXiv:1911.10609), Appendix B, Table VI
# (66 points, in the table's order: row k here is entry k there), an update of
# Kazantzidis & Perivolaropoulos 2018 (arXiv:1803.01337), Table II (63 points).
# Checked against Table VI on 9 October 2026: row 13 (6dFGS) z = 0.067 (was 0.06) and
# row 52 (BOSS DR12, z = 0.56) f sigma_8 = 0.472 (was 0.452, the value of row 53).
# Table VI prints the fiducial Omega_m once per survey block; rows marked "block" below
# have a blank cell and take the value of their block (our reading of the layout).
# Rows 10 - 12 (WiggleZ) are correlated (constants.FS8_WIGGLEZ_COV). Other rows come
# from overlapping galaxy samples (e.g. the BOSS DR12 rows 24, 29 - 34, 37, 38, 46 - 54,
# 64) and are correlated too; Table VI's authors note this, and no covariance is
# available for them, so using all rows together overweights those samples.
